{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"**RESOLVED — value-preserving `terraform apply` completed; drift + this bug cleared. Closing.**\n\nThe close-blocker recorded in the prior \"kept OPEN\" comment (that the only path to a clean apply ran through the `value_wo` cutover, which would clobber all prod SecureStrings to `CHANGEME`) has been eliminated. Under standing operator authorization I executed a **value-PRESERVING** structural `value_wo` migration in the same apply, so no `CHANGEME` window ever existed and no secret was rotated.\n\n**Root cause (proven).** Commit `47383fc18052` (ticket `9015-739e-e72c-4fe5`, \"infra(mcp): materialize per-client bearer PATs\") added `/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-{copilot,codex,claude}` to `local.rebar_secret_params`, which drives the `aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_secrets` `for_each` — declaring the three as **terraform-managed** — but added **no `import` block** for them. The three params had already been operator-seeded out-of-band (v1) in AWS. So on apply the provider issued `PutParameter` with `Overwrite=false` and AWS rejected the create with `ParameterAlreadyExists`, leaving the apply partway and the daily **Terraform Drift** workflow red since 2026-08-25.\n\n**Defect origin / attribution.** `caused_by = 9015-739e-e72c-4fe5`, introducing commit `47383fc18052` (`infra/terraform/ssm.tf`, additions to `local.rebar_secret_params`). Classified **`plan_defect`**: the established adopt-via-import pattern was already in the file (`jira-api-token` had an import block), so the 9015 plan should have shipped matching import blocks for the operator-seeded params; the omission was catchable in review. The `env_integration` flavor (out-of-band seeding) is the manifestation, not the escaped defect — a reviewer following the existing pattern would have caught the missing block.\n\n**Fix (already merged).** Commit `55589c155629` (\"Adopt live mcp-client-pat SSM params via import\", `rebar-ticket: 9350-...`) added the three import blocks mirroring the `jira-api-token` import. Merged to `origin/main` (ancestor-verified) and `Verified +1`.\n\n**Execution + proof (value-preserving apply, this session).**\n- Captured a byte-exact baseline of all 20 managed params (`get-parameters --with-decryption`, JSON-only handling to preserve trailing newlines on ed25519 keys); 19 real values + 1 legitimate `CHANGEME` placeholder (`mcp-tickets-pat`, unseeded).\n- Staged current live values as `value_wo` via a fail-closed var seam (direct map index → hard error on any missing key, never a silent `CHANGEME` fallback; no-default variable → fail-closed if the var-file is absent), so the forced first `value_wo` send wrote back **identical** values.\n- Backed up S3 state (version `QdvCKw_dE9SBRaxTb6FyPiI5j4fe1kgs`; bucket versioning Enabled) before the apply.\n- **Applied: `3 imported, 0 added, 20 changed, 0 destroyed`.**\n- **Verified: all 20 values byte-preserved (post-apply `get-parameters --with-decryption`, sha256 diff = identical for every key), `value_wo_version` 1 on all 20, versions +1.** (`value_wo` is write-only and invisible to `terraform plan`, so the plan cannot prove preservation — the oracle is the post-apply decrypted sha256 re-capture, which confirmed it.)\n- Confirmed the 20 managed slots are now write-only (no cleartext in state).\n- Functional: Gerrit edge HTTP 200; MCP edge HTTP 401 on an unauthenticated probe (auth path intact).\n- Reverted the var-seam edits back to committed config; **`terraform plan` on the committed config with no var-file now reports \"No changes. Your infrastructure matches the configuration.\"** — the `ParameterAlreadyExists` drift and the pending `value_wo` cutover drift are both gone, so the Terraform Drift workflow will return green at steady state.\n\nNo `--force` used anywhere. All cleartext-bearing capture/state artifacts have been shredded; the migration runbook is retained in session state.\n\n**Residual (observed, out of scope — not fixing here):** two `data.aws_ssm_parameter.*` sources (`alert-endpoint`, `google_client_secret`) still read their values into state, and `opcert_origin_guard` (random_password-generated) is legitimately in state. None are migrated managed slots — all 20 managed slots are clean. Noting the data-source-reads-secret-into-state fragility as observed; remediation is out of this ticket's scope.\n\nClosing `in_progress → closed`, class `plan_defect`, `caused_by 9015-739e-e72c-4fe5`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788128610614047514,"uuid":"cbc73aa0-bcfd-4c7b-b288-1d8ffb41f2ac"}